meta {
  name: List a server’s safe reboots, resizes and snapshot-first actions
  type: http
  seq: 29
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/cloud-servers/:cloudServer_id/operations
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  cloudServer_id: 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  The safe reboots, resizes, and rebuilds or deletes that wait for a snapshot first, on this server that are running or finished in the last seven days, newest first. Each lists its steps with their status (`pending`, `running`, `done`, `skipped`, `failed`) and, for a failure, the step and a reason code. A failure that is no longer current says why in `superseded`: `by` is `boot` (the server started again after it) or `operation` (a later operation on the server finished, `kind` naming it), with `at`; `handled_at` and `handled_by` say somebody marked it as handled.

  Scope: `cloud.read`
}
